            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0164" n="112" xml:id="pg112"/>

                <head>52. Memorandum From the Military Assistant to the President’s Assistant for
                    National Security Affairs (Haig) to the
                    Deputy Director of the United States Information Agency (Loomis)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d52-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1969-11-25">November 25, 1969</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Public Opinion Surveys</item>
                </list>
                <p>The President has expressed an interest in learning who actually conducts the
                    public opinion surveys USIA sponsors
                    periodically in foreign countries. Specifically, he would like to know:</p>
                <p>—whether the organizations contracted are subsidiaries of U.S. groups?</p>
                <p>—if it is feasible to use organizations like Gallup and Sidlinger for this sort of survey?</p>
                <p>Would you please send us a memorandum for the President on the above subject.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed corresp="#p_HAM_1">Alexander M.
                            Haig
                        <affiliation>Brigadier General, U.S. Army <lb/> Military
                            Assistant</affiliation></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
